.TH classinfo n 2.0 Tclpp "Tclpp Built-In Commands"
.BS
.SH NAME
classinfo \- Obtain information about classes
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBclassinfo\fR \fIoption\fR ?\fIarg ...\fR?
.SH DESCRIPTION
This command provides information about classes. The legal options (which may 
be abbreviated) are:
.TP
\fBclassinfo classes\fR ?\fIpattern\fR?
Returns a list of fully qualified class names known to the system at
that point. If \fIpattern\fR is specified, only those names are
returned which match the \fIpattern\fR.
.TP
\fBclassinfo heritage\fR \fIclass\fR
Returns a list of the direct base classes of the \fIclass\fR. These
are only the direct parents of this \fIclass\fR, not its entire
lineage.
.TP
\fBclassinfo methods\fR \fIclass\fR
Returns a list of all the methods specified in this \fIclass\fR.
.TP
\fBclassinfo variables\fR \fIclass\fR
Returns a list of all the variables and associated type specified in this
\fIclass\fR.
.LP

.SH AUTHOR(S)
Stefan Sinnige (ssinnige@geocities.com)
.SH SEE ALSO
class(n), objectinfo(n)
